cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FERRUM in research, please cite it as below."
title: "FERRUM: a visualisation core for volumetric medical images"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chukanov
    given-names: Viacheslav
    email: research@vchukanov.ru
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kauter1989/ferrum"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.2
date-released: "2026-10-02"
keywords:
  - medical imaging
  - volume rendering
  - DICOM
  - NIfTI
  - Rust
  - AI agents
abstract: >-
  FERRUM is a reusable visualisation core for volumetric medical images
  (DICOM and NIfTI) written in Rust: a GPU desktop viewer with 2D, MPR and
  3D volume rendering, measurements and segments; an open protocol for
  out-of-process segmentation engines (ferrum-engine/1); and a headless
  command line and MCP server that let AI agents use it as a skill
  (ferrum-agent/1).
